# The build context is `COPY crates ./crates`, so anything under a crate that
# the Rust build does not read is bytes shipped to the daemon for nothing.
#
# The console's toolchain is the whole reason this file exists: `node_modules`
# is hundreds of megabytes and the image needs none of it. What the build *does*
# need is `crates/resonate-gateway-web/assets` — the built app, committed — and
# that is not excluded.
crates/resonate-gateway-web/ui/node_modules/
crates/resonate-gateway-web/ui/.svelte-kit/
crates/resonate-gateway-web/ui/build/

target/
.git/
